{"start":"t:head","attrs":{"{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"en"}}
{"text":"Kiddush for the New Year"}
{"end":"t:head"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"t:note","attrs":{"type":"instruction","facs":"https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n36.jpg","{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"en"}}
{"text":"After the evening prayer but before "}
{"start":"t:foreign","attrs":{"{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"he"}}
{"text":"עלינו"}
{"end":"t:foreign"}
{"tail":" the Kiddush is recited over a glass of wine. At home too, it is recited before the meal, but on the Sabbath preceded by "}
{"start":"t:foreign","attrs":{"{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"he"}}
{"text":"ויכלו"}
{"end":"t:foreign"}
{"end":"t:note"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"j:transclude","attrs":{"type":"external","target":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/text/vayekhulu@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"}}
{"end":"j:transclude"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"j:transclude","attrs":{"type":"external","target":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:borei_peri_hagafen@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"}}
{"end":"j:transclude"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"j:transclude","attrs":{"type":"external","target":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:kiddush_rosh_hashanah@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"}}
{"end":"j:transclude"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"j:transclude","attrs":{"type":"external","target":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:shehecheyanu@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"}}
{"end":"j:transclude"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"t:note","attrs":{"type":"instruction","facs":"https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n36.jpg","{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"en"}}
{"text":"After Kiddush at the meal, one recites "}
{"start":"t:foreign","attrs":{"{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"he"}}
{"text":"המוציא"}
{"end":"t:foreign"}
{"tail":" over the two loaves. After tasting the bread one dips a piece of sweet apple in honey and says:"}
{"end":"t:note"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"j:transclude","attrs":{"type":"external","target":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:borei_peri_haetz@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"}}
{"end":"j:transclude"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"t:note","attrs":{"type":"instruction","facs":"https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n36.jpg","{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"en"}}
{"text":"Then one eats the piece of apple and says:"}
{"end":"t:note"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"j:transclude","attrs":{"type":"external","target":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:shetechaddesh_aleinu_shanah_tovah@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"}}
{"end":"j:transclude"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"t:note","attrs":{"type":"instruction","facs":"https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n36.jpg","{http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace}lang":"en"}}
{"text":"On the eve of the New Year friends and acquaintances express their good wishes to one another in the following phrase:"}
{"end":"t:note"}
{"tail":"\n        "}
{"start":"j:transclude","attrs":{"type":"external","target":"urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/greeting@prayerbook_for_the_new_year-marmorstein-1965-en"}}
